>> Still, though, with bsd ports, you have to deinstall the old version
>> before reinstalling, which whacks this.

>Why so? Is there something in bsd that prevents the Makefile from
>overwriting the old files in the game directory?

The ports have their own Makefiles, which among other things, use a
"patch" target, applying bsd patches to the source.  The native Makefile
is activated as part of the BSD build.

There just isn't an "update" target in the port makefiles.  Ports are
updated, whether manually or automatically, by "make deinstall" to
remove the old, and then "make install" for the new.

It may be possible to change the default behavior so that "install"
would call "update" if nethack is aready installed, but this hasn't been
done.

